// A draft for human review. Every part is described from this repository's own code and docs.

model aerie: Aerie
  > Aerie turns one text model into an interactive architecture diagram that readers can explore
    at different levels of detail.
  @exec: One architecture picture for every audience

audiences exec "Executive", manager "Manager" (default), engineer "Engineer" (code)

system
  repo .

author: Model author | Writes the system model [person]
  > Describes a system in Aerie's Lines language and checks the model as it changes.

reader: Diagram reader | Explores the system picture [person]
  > Opens a view, reads about its parts, follows a scenario or takes a walkthrough.

github: GitHub | Starts pull request checks [external]
  > Hosts the repository and starts Aerie's drift Action for pull requests.

aerie: Aerie | Turns architecture text into diagrams [system]
  code npm:aerie-diagrams
  > The browser viewer, model tools and pull request Action share one TypeScript codebase.
  @exec: Architecture diagrams from one shared model
  @engineer >> The root `package.json` names the package `aerie-diagrams` and exposes
    `src/cli/aerie.ts` as the `aerie` command.

  browser: Browser viewer | Makes a model interactive [service]
    icon web
    > Loads a bundled sample or a local `.aerie` file and presents its diagram in the browser.
    @exec: The interactive architecture picture
    @engineer >> `src/main.ts` starts the page. `src/app/viewer.ts` owns the model picture and
      reader actions; `stage.ts`, `panel.ts`, `scenario.ts`, `presenter.ts`, `travel.ts` and
      `visits.ts` supply its views and controls.

    editor: Live editor | Checks edits and redraws the last good model [module]
      > Lets an author edit a local model beside the diagram, with plain language errors.
      @engineer: | CodeMirror 6, `src/app/split.ts`
      @engineer >> `src/app/live.ts` checks changed text and keeps the last model without errors
        on screen.

  cli: Aerie command line | Checks and serves model files [tool]
    icon gear
    > Checks, formats and prints Lines models, watches a file, and compares a model with code.
    @engineer: | `src/cli/aerie.ts`
    @engineer >> The `check`, `format`, `model`, `watch` and `drift` commands share the language,
      semantics, extraction and drift modules.

  action: GitHub drift Action | Reports model drift on pull requests [tool action]
    icon gear
    > Runs drift checks for configured model files and posts reports and suggested edits to a pull
      request.
    @engineer: | `action.yml`, `src/action/main.ts`
    @engineer >> The composite action runs the shared CLI in process. Its GitHub API adapter and
      comment handling are in `src/action/github.ts` and `src/action/comments.ts`.

  lines: Lines language | Parses and formats architecture text [module]
    > Turns model text into a canonical model and reports language problems with line and column.
    @engineer: | `src/lines/index.ts`
    @engineer >> Exports the parser, formatter, printer, model types, editing helpers and
      diagnostic catalogue. It has no DOM or Node dependency.

  semantics: Model semantics | Resolves what the model means [module]
    > Checks model references and resolves nesting, views, audience wording, scenarios and
      walkthroughs.
    @engineer: | `src/model/index.ts`
    @engineer >> Builds the audience-independent drawing and the wording for each audience; it
      also resolves zoom, scenario trails and walkthrough steps.

  layout: Layout engine | Places every box and relationship [module]
    > Lays out diagrams and scenario lanes while reserving room for every audience's wording.
    @engineer: | `src/layout/index.ts`, ELK behind `src/layout/elk/`
    @engineer >> The browser uses `workerEngine`; the CLI uses `inProcessEngine`. Layout rules and
      readability scores check the resulting pictures.

  renderer: Signal renderer | Draws the diagram as SVG [module]
    > Draws the positioned picture, relationship lines, scenario trails and lanes in the Signal
      look.
    @engineer: | `src/render/index.ts`
    @engineer >> `renderPicture` builds an SVG tree; `signalStyle` writes the visual tokens for
      dark and light themes.

  extractor: Code extractor | Reads supported project files [module]
    > Reads deployment and build files to find code units and connections without running the
      project.
    @engineer: | `src/extract/index.ts`
    @engineer >> Extractors cover Docker Compose, Node packages and Angular, Maven and Spring
      Boot. Project access goes through `ProjectFiles`.

  drift: Drift checker | Compares the model with code facts [module]
    > Finds where a model and the supported facts in a project disagree, then reports evidence and
      suggested edits.
    @engineer: | `src/drift/index.ts`
    @engineer >> Matching, relationship lifting and findings feed the text, diff, JSON and pull
      request report formats.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- relationships

author edits a model in editor
editor sends changed Lines text to semantics
semantics parses and checks model text with lines
semantics gives the checked model to browser
browser requests picture placement from layout
layout sends positioned boxes and routes to renderer
renderer draws the picture for browser
browser shows the picture to reader

author runs model commands with cli
cli checks model text with semantics
cli formats Lines text with lines
cli reads repository facts through extractor
extractor supplies code facts to drift
drift returns findings to cli
cli reports findings to action
github starts action
action runs drift checks through cli
action posts drift findings to github

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- views

view big-picture: Big picture
  show author, browser, cli, action, reader, github
  > Who creates a model, who reads the diagram, and where pull request checks run.

view inside-browser: From model to picture
  show author, browser +1, lines, semantics, layout, renderer, reader
  @exec: How a model becomes a diagram

view code-check: Checking a change against code
  show author, cli, extractor, drift, action, github
  @exec: Catching differences before merge

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- scenarios

scenario render-model: From Lines file to diagram
  > The browser checks a model, lays out its meaning and draws the result for a reader.
  author edits a model in editor
  editor sends changed Lines text to semantics
  semantics parses and checks model text with lines
  semantics gives the checked model to browser
  browser requests picture placement from layout
  layout sends positioned boxes and routes to renderer
  renderer draws the picture for browser
  browser shows the picture to reader

scenario pull-request-drift: Checking a pull request
  > The Action compares each configured model with code facts and reports its findings on GitHub.
  github starts action
  action runs drift checks through cli
  cli reads repository facts through extractor
  extractor supplies code facts to drift
  drift returns findings to cli
  cli reports findings to action
  action posts drift findings to github

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- walkthrough

walkthrough tour: A tour of Aerie
  step big-picture
    > A model author writes one Lines file. A reader explores the resulting picture at their own
      level of detail.
  step inside-browser: editor
    > The live editor checks each change and keeps the last version that worked on screen.
  step inside-browser: lines, semantics
    > The language turns text into a checked model, then semantics resolves its views and flows.
  step inside-browser: layout, renderer
    > Layout places the same picture for every audience, and Signal draws it in the browser.
  step code-check: cli, extractor, drift
    > The command line can compare a model with facts read from supported project files.
  step pull-request-drift: 1-4
    > On a pull request, the Action runs the same check and reports differences on GitHub.
